  "notes": [
    "TemplatePID0245 is patched from checksummed configuration; default PID0245; retain fresh exact runtime HID admission.",
    "GET0F82 request12 [0,5,0x00*10] echoes selector/LED and size; clears responseargs2..11 then fills active state, custom8 explicit, unknownmode actualbyte.",
    "Legacy03/0A targets saved LED5, clears customflag before earlyreturns, and copies full63B record to active; fresh brightness0 reread after effect confirmation required.",
    "Basic legacy destinations: Off[0],Static[6,R,G,B],Breath[3,3]random or[3,count,colors]count1/2,Spectrum[4],Wave[1,wireDirection]fixedspeed40.",
    "0F02 same-effect noops precede RGBchange/flagcleanup: do not use as generic same-effect update.",
    "Frame0F03 args[0,5,row,start,end,RGB...] bounds6x16; max53payload bytes; storagebyte ignored by rowwriter. Stage frame then activate0F02 [0,5,8]. NoframeRGBgetter.",
    "Frame restoration only from captured representable builtin baseline;0F02 storage0 direct baseline restore frommode8 clearscustomflag without saved-bankwrite, thenGET0 confirms typed parameters. Unknown/preexistingcustom8 cannotrestorepixels.",
    "Spectrum getter attests mode only; startup/cycle flag10000264 affects initial palette/phase and is not returned. Noexactphase/pixelrestorationclaim.",
    "No other model inherits this contract; no hardware used.",
    "Static consumer verified:6606 loads active+0B..0D RGB;650C stores runtime+1C..1E;tickmode1->7B1E->762C->754C->74BA. No hidden palette override. Record29/2A are interpolation delay/step.",
    "Breathing77DE count0 uses randompalette;count1/2 branch7834->7878 consumes active+0B+3*index RGB; brightness scales output separately.",
    "Wave wire2 increments phase;wire1 decrements phase (5802..583C), both wrap22. GET returns actualdirection andfixed40.",
    "No fullcustomframe backend implementation reviewed here; source suppliesgeometry,activation,consumer andtypedbuiltin restoration chain, but admission must journal baseline and reject unrepresentable preexisting custom output."
  ],
